course: dictionary
lesson: 14645
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Read the words around the word first. «The detectives walked into the 9th precinct to report the stolen car.» Detectives, report and stolen tell you that precinct means a police station and the area it looks after.
explain: Now read this: «We bought new shoes in the shopping precinct on Saturday.» Shopping tells you that precinct is a place to shop. Cars are not allowed there, so it is an area just for people on foot.
explain: Context can show a third meaning too. «The old church had a quiet garden inside its precinct.» Quiet, garden and church point to the area around a building. Ask yourself: what does the sentence say is near it? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it fits.
fact: Precinct is a noun. Its plural is precincts.
fact: In the USA, a precinct is a district of a city with its own police station, and the police station itself is also called a precinct.
fact: In Britain, a shopping precinct is an area where cars are not allowed.
fact: A precinct can also be the enclosed area around a building, like a cathedral precinct.
fact: In the USA, a precinct can also be a voting district.
exercise: «The detectives walked into the 9th precinct to report the stolen car.» In this sentence, what is a precinct? | *A police station and the district around it | A type of shoe | A kind of car | A dark room
exercise: «We bought new shoes in the shopping precinct, where no cars are allowed.» What is a shopping precinct? | A list of prices | *An area for shopping where cars are not allowed | A kind of shop sign | A road full of traffic
exercise: «The old church had a quiet garden inside its precinct.» What does precinct mean here? | The tall tower on top of the church | The bells that ring on Sunday | *The area around the building | Mud after the rain
test: «The officers worked late at the precinct, writing their reports.» What is the precinct here? | A shopping street where cars are banned | A cathedral garden | *A police station | A bus stop
test: «Mia voted at the local precinct on Tuesday.» What does precinct mean in this sentence? | A police station | A shopping street | *A voting district | A church garden
exam: «Families went to the shopping precinct in town.» What is a shopping precinct in Britain? | A busy road for cars | A police station | A voting place | *A place to shop where cars are not allowed
